powershell script to pull users and groups/security groups associated to users in a easy readable format, and so you can copy+paste

When you run the following command you will get A LOT of info about them
Get-ADUser -Identity adam1234adprofile -Properties memberof -Server hungarian.nerd.com | Select-Object -ExpandProperty memberof 


the following command Filters the output to only display the groups. 
Get-ADUser -Identity 'username' -Properties memberof  -Server 'servername' | Select-Object -ExpandProperty memberof |% {($_.split('=')[1]).split(',')[0]}



if you dont know the server name , you can query it like this;
# 1) Expand HostName to a string
$dc = Get-ADDomainController -Discover -Service ADWS | Select-Object -First 1 -ExpandProperty HostName

# 2) Index explicitly
$dc = (Get-ADDomainController -Discover -Service ADWS).HostName[0]

# 3) Use the PDC emulator (always a single DC)
$dc = (Get-ADDomain).PDCEmulator

Get-ADUser -Identity 'username' -Properties memberof  -Server 'servername' | Select-Object -ExpandProperty memberof |% {($_.split('=')[1]).split(',')[0]}
